---
import MainLayout from '@/layouts/MainLayout.astro';
import { SITE } from '@data/constants';

const pageTitle = `About | ${SITE.title}`;
---

<MainLayout
  title={pageTitle}
  customDescription="About Cloud Architecture and Mark Hughes: hands-on Microsoft 365 and Azure security, mapped to CIS, NIST, ISO 27001, NCSC and NIS2."
>
  <section class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-16 sm:px-6 lg:py-24">
    <div class="flex flex-col items-center text-center">
      <img
        src="/mark.jpg"
        alt="Mark Hughes"
        width="112"
        height="112"
        class="mb-6 h-28 w-28 rounded-full object-cover ring-4 ring-blue-500/20"
      />
      <p
        class="mb-2 text-sm font-bold tracking-wider text-accent uppercase"
      >
        About Cloud Architecture
      </p>
      <h1
        class="mb-4 text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight text-primary md:text-5xl"
      >
        Written by Mark Hughes
      </h1>
      <p
        class="max-w-2xl text-lg text-pretty text-primary"
      >
        Cloud Architecture is a hands-on Microsoft 365 and Azure security
        resource. Every control gets the same treatment: the exact portal
        steps, the reasoning behind them, and the PowerShell to automate it,
        all mapped to CIS, NIST, ISO 27001, NCSC and NIS2.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div
      class="mt-12 space-y-6 text-base leading-relaxed text-primary"
    >
      <p>
        I'm Mark. I build and secure Microsoft 365 and Azure tenants for a
        living. This site is where I write it all down properly: the actual
        click path, why the setting matters, and a re-runnable script so you can
        apply it at scale. Not another checklist that says "enable MFA" and
        leaves you there.
      </p>
      <p>
        Everything here is written for real, production tenants: break-glass
        accounts first, Conditional Access in report-only before you enforce,
        and staged rollouts. The guides work on any Microsoft 365 licence, with
        the licensing caveated per control, and the companion PowerShell is
        idempotent and safe to re-run.
      </p>
      <p>
        If there's a control you'd like covered, or something here you'd do
        differently, I'd genuinely like to hear it.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-10 flex flex-wrap items-center justify-center gap-4">
      <a
        href="/blog"
        class="inline-flex items-center justify-center gap-x-2 rounded-lg bg-blue-600 px-5 py-3 text-sm font-bold text-white transition duration-300 hover:bg-blue-700"
      >
        Read the blog
      </a>
      <a
        href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/markdhughes91/"
        class="inline-flex items-center justify-center gap-x-2 rounded-lg border border-hairline px-5 py-3 text-sm font-bold text-primary transition duration-300 hover:border-blue-500 hover:text-accent"
      >
        LinkedIn
      </a>
      <a
        href="https://github.com/markdhughes"
        class="inline-flex items-center justify-center gap-x-2 rounded-lg border border-hairline px-5 py-3 text-sm font-bold text-primary transition duration-300 hover:border-blue-500 hover:text-accent"
      >
        GitHub
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>
</MainLayout>
